cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use zetesis-puremath in academic work, please cite the entry below (or one of the per-concept-class BibTeX entries in the README)."
title: "zetesis-puremath: A Lean 4 pure-mathematics reservoir"
abstract: >-
  A personal pure-mathematics reservoir in Lean 4 covering six clusters:
  analytic measurability and Choquet capacity on Polish spaces; real-valued
  Kullback--Leibler divergence with binary Pinsker's inequality and mutual
  information; concentration and double-sample exchangeability with a
  Fintype-indexed PMF; multiplicative-weights-update approximate minimax
  for Boolean-matrix games; kernel mean embedding with MMD and HSIC; and
  Assouad's dual VC bound.
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Dhruv
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zetetic-Dhruv/zetesis-puremath"
url: "https://zetetic-dhruv.github.io/zetesis-puremath/"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal mathematics
  - Mathlib
  - measure theory
  - information theory
  - reproducing kernel Hilbert space
  - VC dimension
  - minimax
  - multiplicative weights
year: 2026
